**Clap boundary.** `Cli::parse()` reads the process argument vector and produces the typed command tree. It may print usage/help and terminate on parse failure, so it is not literally pure; the testable form is conceptually `argv → Result<Cli, clap::Error>`.

```rust
Cli { global: GlobalArgs, namespace: Namespace }
Namespace::Openalex(OpenalexArgs {
  cmd: OpenalexCmd::Search { entity, query }
})
GlobalArgs → OutputOpts
```

Only after parsing does `run()` resolve `Config` and match on `cli.namespace`.

**Dispatch contract, not an executing process.** `run_provider` holds `&dyn Provider`; calling `p.dispatch(cmd, opts)` dynamically selects the concrete implementation, here `OpenAlexProvider::dispatch`.

```rust
trait Provider {
  fn dispatch(&self, cmd: ProviderCmd, opts: &OutputOpts)
    -> Result<(Envelope, Emission), ProviderError>;
}
```

Implementations: `OpenAlexProvider`, `ArxivProvider`, `SemanticScholarProvider`, `CrossrefProvider`. OpenCitations still runs a hand-written path in `main.rs`.

OpenalexCmd::Search {
  entity: String,
  query: String,
}

A typed enum value selected from Cli.namespace. No network request has happened.

match oa.cmd {
  OpenalexCmd::Search { entity, query } =>
    ProviderCmd::Search { entity: Some(entity), query },
  // other OpenAlex verbs
}

Local enum-to-enum transformation; no network, store, or stdout effect.

impl Provider for OpenAlexProvider {
  fn dispatch(cmd, opts)
    -> Result<(Envelope, Emission), ProviderError>
}

For Search, it chooses the entity (works by default) and calls openalex::verbs::search(&self.client, …). This is the concrete method selected through &dyn Provider.

impl Provider for ArxivProvider {
  fn dispatch(cmd, opts)
    -> Result<(Envelope, Emission), ProviderError>
}

Dispatches `Get` and `Search` to `arxiv::verbs`; all other shared verbs return `UnsupportedVerb`.
